 "text": "Recorder - Allamakee County, Iowa -->\nRecorder - Allamakee County, Iowa\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser .\nMENU MENU\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nConservation Board\nCounty Social Services\nEmergency Management\nE-911\nEngineer\nEnvironmental Health\nGIS\nPlanning and Development\nRecorder\nRelief\nSheriff’s Office\nSubstance Abuse\nTreasurer\nVeterans’ Affairs\nWaste Management\nBoards & Commissions\nBoard of Supervisors\nBoard of Health\nTownship Officials\nBoard / Commission Openings\nEmployment\nJob Opportunities\nEmployee FMLA Rights\nResources\nNews & Announcements\nCounty Documents\nEvents\nAbout\nContact\nSheriff\nDirectory\nSearch\nRecorder\n-->\nRecorder\nHome Departments Recorder\nThank you for visiting the Allamakee County Recorder's Office Webpage.\nThe basic duty of the County Recorder is to maintain official records of documents affecting title to real estate. Our office also works with vital records, Marriage licenses, DNR licenses, boat, ATV, off-road motorcycles, and snowmobile registrations.\nIt is our goal to provide accurate information to the public, either in person or on-line.\nIndividuals are encouraged to go on-line to research recorded documents at Iowa Land Records for records 1980 to the present instead of doing research in the vault.\nStaff\nKaren Mathis\nCounty Recorder\nMichele Huinker\n1st Deputy\nLindsey Bieber\n2nd Deputy\nDuties\nRecord and maintain documents affecting title to real estate\nRegister and title boats, snowmobiles and ATV's/ORV's/ORM's\nIssue certified copies of vital records (Birth, Death and Marriage)\nIssue Marriage Licenses\nMilitary Service Records\nIssue various types of Hunting and Fishing Licenses\nMiscellaneous Responsibilities\nAdditional Duties\nLocation\nAllamakee County Courthouse\n110 Allamakee St\nWaukon, Iowa 52172\nContact Us\nPhone: 563-568-2364\nFax: 563-568-6419\nEmail: Contact Recorder\nOffice Hours\n8:00 AM to 4:00 PM\nDepartment Information\nRecorder Forms\nFees\nRecorder's Duties\nHistorical Website: Available Now!\nAccess to historical documents dated 1851 - 1979 is now available for public access. You will be required to create a user account and select a subscription option. In county users do not pay a fee.\nView the Records\nHelpful Links\nCode of Iowa\nIowa Department of Health & Human Services\nIowa Department of Revenue\nIowa DNR\nIowa Land Records\nSecretary of State\nEnglish ▼\nArabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish\n110 Allamakee Street Waukon, IA 52172\nMon - Fri 8AM - 4PM\nPhone Directory\nCopyright © 2026 Allamakee County, Iowa. All Rights Reserved. Powered by Iroc Web Design Services .\nTop\n×\nSearch...",
